<%# The record table owns the row and its remove control; this partial supplies
    only the field cells. Name and code live on the transaction code, so the
    object is built as the pair the save path writes.

    Two fields, not ten: a property being set up is saying how guests can hand
    over money, not configuring the till. The accounting code is derived from
    the name, the default cash drawer is settled by the rows themselves, and
    whether the method is accepted is what keeping or removing the row already
    means. A surcharge posts as an extra charge and carries its taxes, which is
    a fee decision rather than an opening one — it stays under Settings, where
    the picker it needs always has something in it.

    The standard codes every property is given — cash, card, bank transfer and
    the two the channel side posts through — read as text rather than fields.
    Renaming or retyping one would break what the rest of the system posts
    through it, and the owner's decision about it is the one the remove control
    already offers: keep it or do not. Only rows they add themselves are typed.

    Everything the table stopped asking for is still carried, hidden: a method
    adopted from a seeded code, or one already configured under Settings, must
    come back out of this form as it went in. What a locked row holds is not
    carried at all — the save path reads it from the record, so a submission
    saying otherwise changes nothing.

    Labels are plain and are not hidden here. At table widths the record table
    hides them itself, because the column header does the naming; below 48rem
    the header row is gone, each row becomes a stacked editor, and these labels
    come back to carry it. A locked cell wears the same label class so it reads
    the same way in both. %>
<% locked = entry["locked"] == "true" %>
<% object = HotelPaymentMethod.new(transaction_code: TransactionCode.new) %>
<% object.assign_attributes(
     name: entry["name"],
     payment_method_type: entry["payment_method_type"].presence || "bank_gateway"
   ) %>
<%= fields_for "payment_method_entries[#{index}]", object do |row_form| %>
  <td>
    <%= row_form.hidden_field :id, value: entry["id"] %>
    <% { "transaction_code_id" => entry["transaction_code_id"],
         "code" => entry["code"],
         "guest_advance" => entry.fetch("guest_advance", "false"),
         "default_cash" => entry.fetch("default_cash", "false"),
         "active" => entry.fetch("active", "true"),
         "surcharge_enabled" => entry.fetch("surcharge_enabled", "false"),
         "surcharge_posting_type" => entry["surcharge_posting_type"],
         "surcharge_value" => entry["surcharge_value"],
         "surcharge_extra_charge_id" => entry["surcharge_extra_charge_id"] }.each do |field, value| %>
      <%= hidden_field_tag "payment_method_entries[#{index}][#{field}]", value %>
    <% end %>
    <%= hidden_field_tag "payment_method_entries[#{index}][_destroy]", "false", data: { record_table_destroy: true } %>

    <% if locked %>
      <div class="panel-form-field">
        <span class="panel-form-field__label">Name</span>
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground"><%= entry["name"] %></p>
      </div>
    <% else %>
      <%= render PanelsUI::FormField.new(form: row_form, attribute: :name, label: "Name",
                                         size: :sm, required: true) do |field| %>
        <% field.with_input(placeholder: "Cash") %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </td>

  <td>
    <% if locked %>
      <div class="panel-form-field">
        <span class="panel-form-field__label">Type</span>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          <%= entry["payment_method_type"] == "cash" ? "Cash" : "Card or bank" %>
        </p>
      </div>
    <% else %>
      <%= render PanelsUI::FormField.new(form: row_form, attribute: :payment_method_type, label: "Type",
                                         size: :sm) do |field| %>
        <% field.with_select_menu(
             [ { label: "Cash", value: "cash" }, { label: "Card or bank", value: "bank_gateway" } ],
             selected: entry["payment_method_type"].presence || "bank_gateway") %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </td>
<% end %>
